  "description": "Coom Wedge Tomb is a prehistoric site, a wedge tomb on the Iveragh Peninsula in County Kerry [1]. It is near the Skellig Ring, a route in the west of the peninsula [1]. The chamber is about 3 metres long, covered by a single slab [1]. There is an open antechamber in front of this, with three large stones on each side, the tallest about 1.5 metres high [1].",
